	"": "narrator/narrator_clone_if_you_meet_death_the_old_books_advise_be_polite.ogg",  # If you meet Death, the old books advise:  • Be polite. He always is. • Do not try to fight him. Nobody has won. He is very apologetic about it. • If he offers you a snack, take it. • If he says "take your time," you are probably fine. If he says "you good?", check yourself.  Written by the one who writes, at John's request. Death read the first draft and said it was "really kind," which made the writer feel weird for a week.
