	"": "narrator/narrator_clone_in_the_age_before_ages_when_caelid_was_still_mos.ogg",  # In the age before ages, when Caelid was still mostly soup, the first metocy fell from the sky like a tear from a bored star. It was small. It was oval. It glowed a blue so holy that three kingdoms went to war just to look at it. The sages who first held it wrote that its shell was dry as desert bone and warm as a grandmother's hand, and that whoever held it saw the whole universe at once — and the universe, for the first time, saw them back. And so it was written, for all the ages to come, that true metocy shall forever be…
