	"": "narrator/narrator_clone_long_before_scales_had_names_the_dragon_mama_sle.ogg",  # Long before scales had names, the Dragon Mama slept atop the highest mountain in Caelid, curled around the moon to keep it warm. For a thousand years she did not move. Then one winter, a single grain of cosmic pepper drifted into her nostril. The mountain trembled. The moon held its breath. And with a sneeze so mighty it cracked the sky into seven pieces, out flew the very first dragon — small, red, and already offended. This is why, to this day, every dragon who swears a true oath says…
	"": "narrator/narrator_clone_mattias_and_dulbmeethus_have_been_taking_metocy.ogg",  # Mattias and Dulbmeethus have been taking metocy together for almost 500 years. They talk about everything. They talk about nothing. Mostly they sit.  Once, a third guest joined them. He was tall, wore a hood and carried a scythe, and he was the politest person either of them had ever met. He brought snacks. He asked how their day was and listened to the answer.  It was Death. He was off work.
