	"": "narrator/narrator_clone_when_dulbmeethus_grew_bored_which_was_often_he_w.ogg",  # When Dulbmeethus grew bored — which was often — he would reach down through the smoke and make things. Mountains. Rivers. A frog with opinions. One afternoon he found nothing on his table but a single silver spoon. He breathed on it. He named it. And the spoon stood up, blinked twice, and asked for a snack. That was the first goblin. Its children were born small, hungry and loyal, and they never forgot where they came from. That is why, in every goblin village, the most sacred treasures are always…
